WEBVTT

00:01.947 --> 00:05.508
- Gee, I'm sorry you have to go.
- I don't have to go.

00:05.684 --> 00:08.414
I mean, I'm sorry I have work to do
so you can't stay.

00:08.587 --> 00:10.885
Didrt you hear me? I can stay.

00:11.557 --> 00:14.185
Yeah, I wish you could.

00:16.395 --> 00:19.796
But there's no way
I'd be able to concentrate with you around.

00:20.799 --> 00:23.461
Don't forget your sweater.

00:23.635 --> 00:25.899
You know, you are so thoughtful.
Most guys aren't.

00:26.071 --> 00:28.631
Most guys are selfish bastards
who just wanna use you...

00:28.807 --> 00:30.866
...and throw you away. Heh.

00:32.778 --> 00:34.871
Damn them.

00:35.781 --> 00:37.646
Anything else you have might overlooked?

00:37.816 --> 00:41.479
Cell phone, earrings, any medications?

00:42.955 --> 00:45.924
Hang on. Nope, I'm all set.

00:46.558 --> 00:49.652
Good, good.
Okay, well, I'll see you soon.

00:49.828 --> 00:51.693
- How soon?
- Very soon.

00:51.863 --> 00:53.558
- So you'll call?
- What do you think?

00:53.732 --> 00:56.257
- I think you'll call.
- Well, there you go.

00:59.137 --> 01:00.399
So when will you call?

01:00.572 --> 01:01.698
- Soon.
- How soon?

01:01.873 --> 01:04.103
We're back on this ride, huh?

01:04.643 --> 01:06.201
Okay, very soon. Bye-bye, now.

01:12.718 --> 01:15.278
- Ah. When will I learn?
Soon.

01:17.389 --> 01:18.788
Very soon.

01:19.224 --> 01:23.024
Don't tell me.
Tell the cockeyed optimist in my pants.

01:23.729 --> 01:26.789
- So where'd you find this one?
- The animal shelter.

01:27.866 --> 01:31.700
- Are we getting a pet?
- Are you crazy? We've already got your kid.

01:33.639 --> 01:35.197
Then what were you doing there?

01:35.374 --> 01:38.810
Standing within earshot
of attractive women and mumbling:

01:38.977 --> 01:41.537
"Gee, I wish I could adopt them all. "

01:43.148 --> 01:45.548
It's foolproof.

01:46.084 --> 01:48.416
There's something
that I need to talk to you about.

01:48.587 --> 01:50.919
You know the difference
between you and me, Alan?

01:51.089 --> 01:55.287
- I don't scream when I pee?
- I took care of that.

01:56.995 --> 02:00.089
No, the difference between you and me
is I have vision.

02:00.265 --> 02:03.462
- I see what others don't.
- Terrific. The thing I wanted to tell you...

02:03.635 --> 02:05.102
You look at an animal shelter...

02:05.270 --> 02:08.364
...and see homeless dogs
and kitties about to be put to death.

02:08.540 --> 02:11.509
Me? I see an ass farm.

02:12.177 --> 02:13.838
Okay, I'm speechless.

02:14.913 --> 02:18.144
No words necessary.
Silent admiration is all I ask.

02:20.152 --> 02:23.349
So, what is it you wanted to tell me?

02:28.160 --> 02:30.355
The railing's a little loose.

02:40.806 --> 02:44.207
Ah. I gotta stop falling off the deck sober.

02:57.622 --> 02:59.385
Morning. How are you feeling?

03:00.192 --> 03:04.492
Like I fell 8 feet onto splintered wood
and wet sand and a dead crab.

03:04.863 --> 03:08.731
One would think your highly inflated ego
might have broken your fall.

03:09.367 --> 03:12.928
So where'd you find Pancho Bob villa
out there?

03:14.539 --> 03:17.007
You know those fliers
that get left in your mailbox?

03:17.175 --> 03:18.472
- Yeah.
- Well, I take them...

03:18.643 --> 03:21.339
...and file them according to category.

03:22.614 --> 03:26.106
Takeout menus, rug sales,
carpet cleaning, plumbing, tiling.

03:26.284 --> 03:29.617
Fernando was under
"handyman services. "

03:31.056 --> 03:33.490
You're gonna live here forever,
aren't you?

03:34.693 --> 03:37.924
He's licensed, he's bonded, he's punctual,
and he's reasonably priced.

03:38.096 --> 03:39.188
Are you paying him?

03:39.364 --> 03:42.390
No, but I'm saving you 20 percent
with this valuable coupon.

03:44.302 --> 03:45.326
Morning.

03:45.504 --> 03:46.493
- Hey.
- Morning.

03:48.039 --> 03:49.165
What in the heck is...?

03:49.341 --> 03:51.309
Oh, yum.

03:53.111 --> 03:56.137
- Who is that?
- He's a handyman.

03:56.615 --> 03:59.641
Ooh. Nice. Can we keep him?
Can we? Can we?

03:59.818 --> 04:01.547
He's just here to fix the deck.

04:01.720 --> 04:04.951
Great, there's a lot of work
that can be done in here too.

04:05.123 --> 04:06.488
Like what?

04:06.658 --> 04:10.594
Well, for starters,
that cabinet door is coming off its hinges.

04:10.762 --> 04:12.195
Really?

04:18.003 --> 04:19.834
No, it's not.

04:26.111 --> 04:28.238
Yeah, it is.

04:31.750 --> 04:36.244
He looks parched. I'll take him some rum.

04:40.892 --> 04:43.554
See, my problem is, is that I'm a giver.

04:43.728 --> 04:47.596
I love too much,
and it's always the wrong man.

04:48.333 --> 04:52.167
- You have romance in your heart.
- Oh, I have romance all over me.

04:52.337 --> 04:54.669
I reek of it.

04:54.840 --> 04:57.274
&lt;i>- Another mojito?
- Oh, no.&lt;/i>

04:57.442 --> 04:59.774
One is my limit
when I work with power tools.

04:59.945 --> 05:00.969
That's smart.

05:01.146 --> 05:04.513
We wouldn't want you
to lose one of those beautiful thumbs.

05:05.317 --> 05:07.547
- Berta.
- What?

05:07.886 --> 05:10.150
L... I just thought
that maybe it's almost lunchtime...

05:10.322 --> 05:13.689
&lt;i>oh, yeah. Quesadilla, bright eyes?&lt;/i>

05:13.859 --> 05:16.419
- Thank you.
- Coming up.

05:16.595 --> 05:19.496
&lt;i>- Actually, I'd rather have a sandwich.
- I'm making quesadillas.&lt;/i>

05:19.664 --> 05:20.961
&lt;i>Quesadilla's fine.&lt;/i>

05:23.134 --> 05:26.626
So, Fernando, how's it going?

05:26.805 --> 05:29.501
I'm sorry to tell you this,
but you have a problem here.

05:29.674 --> 05:33.201
Just don't let her corner you
in the laundry room and you'll be fine.

05:33.578 --> 05:35.205
No, the deck.

05:35.380 --> 05:38.213
- Whers the last time you put sealant on it?
- Well...

05:38.383 --> 05:39.475
Uh...

05:40.118 --> 05:41.142
What?

05:41.686 --> 05:44.883
Oh, señor, you cannot have wood untreated
this close to the ocean.

05:45.056 --> 05:47.820
The moisture,
she gets in and rots it from the inside.

05:48.393 --> 05:50.190
Where have I heard that before?

05:50.362 --> 05:54.389
Right, my doctor.
But it wasrt moisture, it was Scotch.

05:54.566 --> 05:57.000
You need to replace the railing,
parts of the deck...

05:57.168 --> 05:58.829
...and the stairway to the beach.

05:59.004 --> 06:02.906
Oh. Well, why can't I just
put on some of that sealant?

06:03.074 --> 06:05.941
You could do that,
but it would be, as we say:

06:07.545 --> 06:10.844
- What's that mean?
- Milking a dead cow.

06:11.716 --> 06:12.705
Ah.

06:13.752 --> 06:17.347
Well, uh, maybe before I commit
to all this work...

06:17.522 --> 06:19.353
...I should get a second opinion.

06:19.524 --> 06:23.688
I understand.
You're a smart and careful man.

06:26.631 --> 06:29.623
But I would hurry up,
before your deck falls off.

06:30.969 --> 06:33.267
Something else my doctor told me.

06:37.943 --> 06:39.410
Hello?

06:39.744 --> 06:40.733
Oh, uh...

06:40.912 --> 06:43.642
Hang on, I'll... I'll see if he's here.

06:44.516 --> 06:45.915
It's Chloe.

06:48.053 --> 06:50.078
I need more than that, Alan.

06:51.189 --> 06:53.214
The girl you adopted
at the animal shelter.

06:55.126 --> 06:57.890
- God, she won't leave me alone.
- What do you want me to say?

06:58.063 --> 07:01.226
- I don't know, tell her I'm sick.
- Okay.

07:02.100 --> 07:03.727
What do you have?

07:04.402 --> 07:07.565
- What are you talking about?
- Well, are you bedridden or ambulatory?

07:09.607 --> 07:12.269
- Uh, bedridden.
- Got it.

07:13.745 --> 07:17.306
- Is it viral or bacterial?
- What?

07:17.482 --> 07:20.315
Well, if I'm gonna lie convincingly,
I need details.

07:20.485 --> 07:24.285
- I don't know, I got a bug.
- Intestinal or bronchial?

07:25.357 --> 07:29.054
- Just tell her I got the flu, all right?
- Oh, good, the flu.

07:29.527 --> 07:30.789
Is it coming out both ends?

07:32.063 --> 07:34.588
Just give me the freaking phone.

07:38.269 --> 07:41.102
No. It's okay, I wanna talk to her.

07:43.108 --> 07:45.133
Hello, Chloe.

07:46.044 --> 07:49.275
No, I'm fine. Just a little bug.

07:49.447 --> 07:51.711
Doctor said I should be okay
in a couple of weeks.

07:53.084 --> 07:56.281
Me too, baby. I'll call you.

07:56.454 --> 07:58.285
Soon.

07:59.657 --> 08:01.887
Very soon.

08:02.060 --> 08:04.290
See? Was that so hard?

08:04.462 --> 08:08.489
Well, to be fair, you had the advantage
of making it a performance piece.

08:09.667 --> 08:10.691
Hey, dogs.

08:10.869 --> 08:12.029
- Hey.
- Hey, Jake.

08:12.203 --> 08:16.139
Alan, here, I need you to sign these papers
for Jake's summer school.

08:16.307 --> 08:20.073
- Oh, summer school again?
- Why not? He's getting good at it.

08:20.245 --> 08:23.078
Oh, my Lord. Who is that?

08:24.082 --> 08:27.381
- He's my handyman.
- I've been looking for a good handyman.

08:27.552 --> 08:30.419
- It's a little soon to know how good he is.
- I'll find out.

08:32.424 --> 08:34.858
I'm starting to see a trend here.

08:44.869 --> 08:46.496
That bony bitch.

08:53.511 --> 08:55.342
Yep, definitely a trend.

08:59.918 --> 09:02.887
Summer school three years in a row.

09:03.054 --> 09:05.614
They might as well
just make you the janitor.

09:07.992 --> 09:11.792
- Ah, well, school sucks.
- That's because you go year-round.

09:13.198 --> 09:16.531
Imagine if you had a couple of months off
in the summer.

09:16.701 --> 09:20.762
If I were you, I'd start teaching him
how to throw sawdust on vomit.

09:21.272 --> 09:22.899
I could do that.

09:23.842 --> 09:25.776
Why don't you just
go start your homework?

09:25.944 --> 09:28.105
What's the point?
I'm already going to summer school.

09:28.279 --> 09:30.440
- Jake.
- And if I flunk there, what can they do?

09:30.615 --> 09:33.607
- Send me to regular school?
- Go.

09:35.620 --> 09:38.487
Actually, that sawdust job
might be a pipe dream.

09:42.193 --> 09:43.217
Is the big one gone?

09:45.130 --> 09:47.428
Yeah, she went to get something waxed.

09:48.766 --> 09:51.166
We were scared to ask what.

09:51.603 --> 09:54.868
I just wanted to tell you I was able
to save you money on the redwood.

09:55.039 --> 09:56.734
- That's terrific. How?
- My cousin.

09:56.908 --> 09:59.809
He works at a lumberyard and...

10:00.612 --> 10:02.136
That's all you need to know.

10:02.881 --> 10:05.975
- Well, thanks.
- No problem. I'll get back to work.

10:06.851 --> 10:09.411
- I like this guy.
- Course you do.

10:09.587 --> 10:13.023
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Charlie, he's a younger version of you.

10:14.359 --> 10:15.690
Oh, yeah, that must be it.

10:17.028 --> 10:21.260
I'll get it.
- There you go. He could be a doorman.

10:22.100 --> 10:24.364
- I don't appreciate...
- I'm not saying right away.

10:24.536 --> 10:27.096
He could work his way up from doorstop.

10:27.572 --> 10:28.869
Uncle Charlie, it's Chloe.

10:29.040 --> 10:32.407
- Aw, jeez, did you let her in?
- No, she's on the front porch.

10:32.577 --> 10:34.943
- I told her I'd see if you were home.
- Thattaboy.

10:35.313 --> 10:37.611
See? He'll make doorman in no time.

10:38.783 --> 10:42.048
- She brought soup.
- Why would she bring soup?

10:42.220 --> 10:45.451
You told her you had a bug,
so she assumed it was bronchial.

10:45.623 --> 10:49.753
If you'd been more specific like I suggested,
you could have precluded this.

10:50.562 --> 10:53.725
Nobody just drops by
when they think you have diarrhea.

10:56.201 --> 10:59.295
And I bet they don't bring soup, either.

11:00.071 --> 11:01.698
All right, all right.

11:01.873 --> 11:05.468
I'm gonna sneak out the back door.
Just tell her I had a doctor's appointment.

11:05.643 --> 11:06.735
G.P. Or specialist?

11:08.746 --> 11:13.308
Alan, I swear to God, I will rip off your head
and use your neck as a bedpan.

11:13.918 --> 11:18.150
- You cannot keep lying to this girl forever.
- Oh, I think I can.

11:18.323 --> 11:21.315
Go out there, tell her you're not interested
in a relationship...

11:21.492 --> 11:23.392
...and be done with it.

11:23.561 --> 11:26.997
Yeah. I guess you're right.

11:27.165 --> 11:29.258
I say we eat the soup before you tell her.

11:32.737 --> 11:34.705
Smelled like minestrone.

11:35.273 --> 11:37.264
Listen, Chloe, we need to talk.

11:39.577 --> 11:40.566
Chloe?

11:47.452 --> 11:49.010
Looks like your problem's solved.

11:49.187 --> 11:52.953
Are you crazy?
That rat bastard is stealing my girlfriend.

11:54.959 --> 11:57.587
Forget the girl, he's stealing our soup.

12:03.868 --> 12:06.530
Hey, baby, thanks so much
for coming to see me.

12:06.704 --> 12:09.537
Yeah, well, that's what friends are for.

12:11.276 --> 12:14.040
So, um, Charlie,
did you know that Fernando volunteers...

12:14.212 --> 12:16.703
...to build homeless shelters
in his spare time?

12:16.881 --> 12:21.409
No, I didn't.
Did you know his cousin steals wood?

12:22.253 --> 12:25.620
Really? That is fascinating.

12:25.990 --> 12:28.652
Why don't you come on inside
so we can visit?

12:29.093 --> 12:32.722
- I'll see you later, Fernando.
- Thank you for your thoughtful soup.

12:32.897 --> 12:36.060
It nourishes my body
as your beauty nourishes my soul.

12:40.271 --> 12:42.637
Find something to saw.

12:44.008 --> 12:46.476
So, Chloe, what's new?

12:46.644 --> 12:50.944
Huh? Oh, nothing.
What is he, like, Colombian?

12:51.749 --> 12:53.046
I don't know.

12:53.217 --> 12:55.777
But I gotta tell you,
I do feel much better seeing you.

12:56.421 --> 12:59.913
God, it's like his eyes are looking
inside your soul.

13:01.326 --> 13:03.920
Yeah. Kind of creepy.

13:04.462 --> 13:07.090
The way he speaks, it's so romantic.

13:09.967 --> 13:11.958
Hey, I almost forgot.

13:12.737 --> 13:14.796
- I wrote you a song.
- Really?

13:14.972 --> 13:16.701
Well, you've been on my mind a lot...

13:16.874 --> 13:19.468
...and I wanted to find a way
to express my feelings.

13:19.644 --> 13:20.770
What's it called?

13:21.512 --> 13:22.604
Uh...

13:23.114 --> 13:24.604
"Chloe's Song. "

13:26.551 --> 13:29.315
I haven't put any words to it yet,
but it goes something like this.

13:40.698 --> 13:42.165
&lt;i>FERNANDo:
Can't you see?&lt;/i>

13:44.802 --> 13:48.465
&lt;i>You're everything I hoped for&lt;/i>

13:48.639 --> 13:51.130
&lt;i>You're everything I need&lt;/i>

13:53.344 --> 13:59.078
&lt;i>You are so beautiful&lt;/i>

14:00.785 --> 14:02.980
&lt;i>To me&lt;/i>

14:04.455 --> 14:07.481
You should use those words.

14:16.467 --> 14:19.368
- Thanks again for stopping by.
- Yeah, I'm glad you're feeling better.

14:19.537 --> 14:21.903
- So when am I gonna see you again?
- Soon.

14:22.640 --> 14:26.235
- How soon?
- I'll call you. Bye, Fernando.

14:28.913 --> 14:30.346
Oh, God.

14:33.484 --> 14:35.577
Call me.

14:38.055 --> 14:42.389
- You have a beautiful lady, Señor Harper.
- Thank you.

14:42.827 --> 14:46.285
She must make you feel,
how do you say...

14:47.598 --> 14:48.690
...young again?

14:53.438 --> 14:56.965
Yeah. That's what I'm feeling.

14:58.276 --> 15:02.178
Oh. Hey, Charlie, I was thinking, uh,
after Fernando's done with the deck...

15:02.346 --> 15:05.247
...he could patch that hole in the roof
where the squirrels get in.

15:05.416 --> 15:07.213
- I don't think so.
- Why not?

15:07.652 --> 15:08.880
I like squirrels.

15:10.888 --> 15:12.480
Hey, me too.

15:13.758 --> 15:17.057
But they get into the crawlspace,
where they breed and die.

15:17.228 --> 15:19.423
That's what I like about them, Alan.

15:21.365 --> 15:23.629
I like their little hands.

15:23.801 --> 15:25.928
Uh, come on, Charlie,
all Fernando would have to do...

15:26.103 --> 15:27.968
Forget Fernando.

15:28.139 --> 15:30.937
I'm having second thoughts
about him even finishing the deck.

15:31.108 --> 15:34.441
- What? You wanna fire him?
- I don't want to.

15:34.612 --> 15:36.910
I just don't think his work
is very professional.

15:37.081 --> 15:38.708
I mean, he's wasting a lot of wood.

15:38.883 --> 15:41.010
And, you know,
wood just doesn't grow on tree...

15:41.185 --> 15:42.652
He's gotta go.

15:42.820 --> 15:45.254
Charlie, you're not fooling anybody.
You're... You're jealous.

15:45.656 --> 15:46.782
Jealous?

15:46.958 --> 15:51.258
You know what's cooler than squirrels?
Anteaters. They're just crazy-looking.

15:53.397 --> 15:54.762
I'm not jealous.

15:54.932 --> 15:57.127
And their name tells you
what to feed them.

15:59.704 --> 16:01.262
Why would you say I'm jealous?

16:01.439 --> 16:03.771
I'm an omnivore.
That means I eat anything.

16:03.941 --> 16:06.409
Yeah, we've noticed. Now shut up.

16:07.044 --> 16:08.443
I'm not jealous.

16:08.613 --> 16:11.605
You wanna fire this guy
because he's younger and better-looking.

16:11.782 --> 16:13.215
And he can sing.

16:13.384 --> 16:16.182
This has nothing to do with that.
And I can sing too.

16:16.354 --> 16:18.185
Yeah, but you stink.

16:21.225 --> 16:23.557
I am done for the day.
I'll see you in the morning?

16:23.728 --> 16:25.025
Hold on, Fernando.

16:25.196 --> 16:28.222
- I wanna talk to you.
- Yes?

16:30.167 --> 16:33.967
- Never mind. Good night.
- Is there a problem?

16:34.138 --> 16:36.470
Because I want everything
to be perfect for you.

16:36.641 --> 16:40.702
You're a good man and I respect you.
You remind me of my sainted father.

16:43.514 --> 16:44.742
Thank you.

16:44.916 --> 16:48.317
He was wise and strong,
until syphilis made him crazy.

16:50.454 --> 16:53.855
Again, thanks. Good night.

16:59.564 --> 17:04.501
I thought you were gonna get rid of him.
Or did you go crazy there for a second?

17:05.570 --> 17:08.368
I don't know, I just... I just couldn't.

17:08.539 --> 17:10.268
Yeah, I think it's his eyes.

17:10.441 --> 17:14.036
- It's like they're looking right into my soul.
- That's what Mom said.

17:15.613 --> 17:19.811
- Women used to say that about my eyes.
- Really?

17:19.984 --> 17:22.851
Because now they're kind of milky
and bloodshot.

17:24.455 --> 17:28.619
Actually, the... The one on the right
is starting to look a little lazy.

17:28.793 --> 17:32.752
- You know, you're right.
- Okay, okay, that's enough.

17:32.930 --> 17:36.127
Come on, Charlie, you can't expect
to compete with a guy half your age.

17:36.300 --> 17:37.631
I am not competing.

17:37.802 --> 17:39.895
Well, you shouldn't,
because it's perfectly natural.

17:40.071 --> 17:43.131
Each generation passes the torch on
to the next.

17:43.741 --> 17:48.007
The child becomes the hunter.
The hunter becomes the revered elder.

17:48.179 --> 17:51.979
When you're too old to chase the buffalo,
it's time to stay back with the old women...

17:52.149 --> 17:54.276
...and make necklaces.

17:55.853 --> 17:56.877
Necklaces?

17:57.054 --> 17:59.955
Or weave blankets, tend the fire...

18:00.124 --> 18:02.319
...teach the kids to whittle.

18:04.028 --> 18:07.327
Buffalos are cool too.
They're like badass cows.

18:17.475 --> 18:21.377
- Charlie.
- Yeah, hi.

18:21.545 --> 18:25.276
I was just in the neighborhood
and thought I'd drop off your soup Thermos.

18:25.449 --> 18:29.078
Thanks. What did you do to yourself?

18:29.253 --> 18:32.450
Me? Nothing, nothing.
I was just doing a little work outdoors.

18:32.623 --> 18:35.091
- Got some sun.
- Oh.

18:35.259 --> 18:37.124
What's up with your teeth?

18:37.294 --> 18:40.525
Oh, I just brushed them real good.

18:41.832 --> 18:43.265
So can I come in?

18:43.434 --> 18:46.164
Oh, gee, Charlie, I really...

18:46.337 --> 18:48.498
...wish you would've called.
FERNANDo: Oh.

18:48.673 --> 18:50.641
Señor Harper...

18:55.413 --> 18:59.144
- I was, how do you say...?
- About to sleep with my girlfriend?

19:00.051 --> 19:02.485
Okay, about to.

19:05.289 --> 19:07.553
I am so sorry.

19:08.159 --> 19:09.854
I would understand if you fired me.

19:14.732 --> 19:19.192
Hey, it's no big deal, pal.
This is the natural course of events.

19:19.370 --> 19:22.999
You're the next generation:
Young, vibrant, good-looking.

19:23.174 --> 19:26.974
- You can buy Chloe expensive jewelry.
- I cannot buy her expensive jewelry.

19:27.144 --> 19:30.580
Oh, right, that's me.

19:31.115 --> 19:33.481
What do you say, Chloe?
Wanna go shopping?

19:33.651 --> 19:35.482
I'll go get my purse.

19:39.056 --> 19:42.253
And, yeah, you're fired.

19:50.234 --> 19:52.429
Charlie, when are you coming
back to bed?

19:52.937 --> 19:55.337
- Soon.
- How soon? Hee-hee.

19:55.940 --> 19:57.100
I'll be right up, baby.

20:02.980 --> 20:05.642
Okay, let me see if I got this right.

20:06.117 --> 20:09.109
You bought diamonds
for the girl you were trying to get rid of...

20:09.286 --> 20:12.016
...in order to win her
from the handyman you fired.

20:12.189 --> 20:14.623
I'm sensing some judgment here.

20:15.926 --> 20:17.860
You're very astute.

20:18.662 --> 20:22.325
Okay, first of all,
I got Fernando another job.

20:22.500 --> 20:24.900
But the most important thing
to remember is...

20:25.669 --> 20:27.193
...I won.

20:27.638 --> 20:28.969
You're a lecherous old guy...

20:29.140 --> 20:32.166
...who bought a young womars affection
with shiny baubles.

20:32.343 --> 20:35.801
True. But I won.

20:41.285 --> 20:43.253
Are you sure
we cannot open up a window?

20:43.654 --> 20:45.178
No, I like it hot.

20:51.562 --> 20:55.328
Okay, well,
time for the victor to reap the spoils.

20:56.033 --> 20:58.194
Oh, Charlie, aren't you ashamed?

20:58.369 --> 21:01.827
Alan, you know the difference
between you and me?

21:14.685 --> 21:19.645
Yeah, I wouldn't fire the handyman
before he finishes.

21:20.224 --> 21:22.920
Hey, I can see your teeth from up here.
